"""
================================================================================
MASTER CLOCK = (FIBER trimmed & re-zero) == (REAL VIDEO TIME from BehData trimmed & re-zero)

Video file timeline may be "compressed" (e.g., forced 20 fps) -> DO NOT trust its clock.
We build a REAL video-time axis from BehData (frame -> real seconds).

What you asked for:
- ALL tunable "magic values" are gathered in ONE CONFIG block at the top.
- Values are "human-tunable" (avoid 1e-6 style where possible for knobs; tiny eps stays internal).
- For ALL MedPC points:
    * report which video second they correspond to (REAL video time + DISPLAYED video time)
    * report how close/far to nearest manual anchor (distance in seconds + label)
- Prints a console report AND writes CSVs.

Pipeline
--------
0) Read BehData.csv: rows are frames; Onset is real time (s) for each frame.
1) Read video frame PTS (ffprobe best_effort_timestamp_time) => displayed timeline per frame.
2) Build mapping:
   displayed_time -> frame_idx (via ffprobe PTS)
   frame_idx -> real_time (via BehData Onset)
   => displayed_time -> real_time
   and inverse real_time -> frame_idx.
3) Manual anchors are annotated on DISPLAYED (compressed) timeline mm:ss.mmm.
   Convert each anchor to REAL time via displayed->frame->BehData.
   Then apply TRIM_START_SEC (real-time trimming) and re-zero => MASTER axis.
4) MedPC events -> seconds -> (optional cluster)
5) Align manual(MASTER) to MedPC via coarse affine + featured DP.
6) Fiber peri-event uses corrected MedPC times in MASTER.
7) Clip writing uses MASTER == REAL-video (trimmed) -> frame idx (BehData) -> actual video frames.
================================================================================
"""

